From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: negotiate DSC and recover over the attached link

Keep PPS in atomic bridge state. Use DRM link-status/hotplug handling for
attached policy transitions and bounded uncompressed recovery. Retain the
failed DSC latch until a new connection or explicit policy request. Confirm
receiver decoder and FEC configuration readback; monitor the active receiver
and lane status without treating a write ACK as a visible picture.

Source comparison: Uke OEM display 44275c404a677d9d9e5230fedd1af2ef02fc7b9a,
SM7675 OnePlus display 1138e00fee63582a0cc6a53af3286621786827b7, and upstream
Linux 7.3 DP atomic/link-status handling. No board-specific values transferred.
AUX/state validation cannot detect every decoded-pixel error. Physical camera
and transport qualification remain separate from source/build results.

Signed-off-by: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>

